From: mastergray <mastergray@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] expose mixer rate and throttle state to the browser audio probe

Keep the stock JavaScript sound-module boundary intact while forwarding the
configured mixer rate and current throttle state alongside its PCM address and
frame count.  The generic pre-JavaScript probe uses these values to distinguish
the native mixer contract from wall-clock observations.

--- a/src/osd/modules/sound/js_sound.c
+++ b/src/osd/modules/sound/js_sound.c
@@ -37,2 +37,2 @@
-		jsmess_update_audio_stream($0, $1);
-		}, (unsigned int)buffer, samples_this_frame);
+		jsmess_update_audio_stream($0, $1, $2, $3);
+		}, (unsigned int)buffer, samples_this_frame, sample_rate(), is_throttled ? 1 : 0);
